Third-party notice
------------------

The following functions re-implement the documented behaviour of Simple
Machines Forum 2.x, which is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License. They
are independent Rust implementations written from the behaviour the templates
expect; no SMF source text is copied.

- `format_time()` (the `timeformat()` user/forum offset and
  "Today"/"Yesterday" rules)
- `SmfFunctions::call()` entries `create_button`, `allowedto`,
  `theme_inline_permissions`, `theme_copyright`, `comma_format`,
  `timeformat`, `cleanXml` and `JavaScriptEscape`

